From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nowon <nowon@noreply.pepecoin.surf>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:00:07 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 161/162] GreatDANE: F1-F5 StaticPrefs group, atomic types,
 best_known, apply script

F1: keep greatdane.node.lazy / lazyTimeoutSec and add "greatdane" to
pref_groups (moz.build.patch) so StaticPrefs_greatdane.h is generated
and exported. Least invasive way to keep internal greatdane.* names.
F2: RelaxedAtomicBool / RelaxedAtomicInt32; the C++ [1, 60] clamp is
unchanged.
F3: drop bestKnownOk from full mode; lazy applies height+2 >=
best_known_height only when namespace_sync_basis === "offline". Tests
prove a hostile tip does not stall full mode or online-lazy.
F4: drop the .inc.yaml fragment. apply-greatdane-static-prefs.sh
applies the yaml + moz.build patches to a Firefox tree and fails
loudly if the result is missing the prefs or group. A stub test
dry-runs --check on the real tree and applies to a temp copy.
F5: honour lazyAllowPreActivation only under Cu.isInAutomation; if
the pref is set outside automation it is ignored, logged, and shown
on about:dane.

M2, M4 and M5 stay deferred (no mach). Local only, not pushed.
